        "why": "Histones carry a positive charge and DNA a negative one, which is why the DNA wraps tightly round the outside of the octamer. The book's text says 200 bp are wrapped round the core while its own figure says 146 — 146 bp is the wrapped length, and about 200 bp is the repeating unit once the linker is counted.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the octamer has eight different histones. It has four types, two copies each.",
